    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A roof replacement in Utah is typically needed when the roof reaches 20 to 30 years of age or shows widespread structural and material wear.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "when the roof reaches 20 to 30 years of age or shows widespread structural and material wear"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Signs You Need a New Roof"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Age over 20 years: Most asphalt shingle roofs in Utah last 20 to 25 years. If yours is approaching or past this age, materials break down quickly."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Curling, cracking, or missing shingles: Shingles that curl at the edges or cup upward fail to seal out water, making them vulnerable to Utah's freeze-thaw winter cycles."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Granules in the gutters: Finding piles of sand-like granules in your gutters or downspouts means your shingles are losing their protective coating."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Sagging or a wavy roofline: A dipping roof deck or sagging areas point to severe moisture damage and rotting in the wooden decking underneath."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Damaged or rusted flashing: Cracked, rusted, or lifted metal flashing around chimneys and vents frequently causes major winter leaks."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Persistent leaks and water stains: Recurring water stains on ceilings or damp insulation in the attic mean patching is no longer enough."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Widespread moss or algae: Heavy moss and dark streaks hold moisture against the roofing materials, rotting the structure below."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Spiking energy bills: A failing roof system loses proper insulation and ventilation, leading to higher heating and cooling costs."
          }
        ]
      },
